---
// Scan-read summary of the 0.5.0 CHANGELOG entry. Not the full changelog —
// links out to that on GitHub for the rest.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = "What's new in usagio 0.5.0";
const description =
  'usagio 0.5.0 fixes the /login loop for good, adds real Linux and Windows support, Codex switching, a menu redesign, and adaptive poll cadence.';

const github = 'https://github.com/MattJackson/usagio';
const changelog = `${github}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/whats-new/">

  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="wn-hero">
    <div class="container container-narrow" style="text-align: center;">
      <span class="eyebrow fade-up">v0.5.0 — the never-re-login release</span>
      <h1 class="h-display fade-up" style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); margin-top: 0.5rem;">What changed</h1>
      <p class="lede fade-up" style="margin: 1rem auto 0;">
        v0.4.x soak testing surfaced a real pattern: users getting prompted to
        <code>/login</code> in Claude Code despite capturing the account
        weeks earlier. Adversarial audits traced it to usagio refreshing the
        active account's single-use OAuth token out from under Claude Code.
        0.5.0 fixes that at the root, and ships real Linux + Windows support
        alongside it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FIXED ============ -->
  <section class="wn-section">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <h2 class="h-section fade-up">Fixed — the north-star bug</h2>
      <ul class="wn-list fade-up">
        <li>
          <strong>Never-re-login contract now holds.</strong> usagio no longer
          refreshes the ACTIVE account's OAuth token — Claude Code owns that
          slot and rotates it itself; usagio only reads it. Inactive accounts
          still refresh automatically, and every rotation is mirrored back to
          the vendor CLI's OS-native storage (Keychain on macOS, a plain file
          on Linux and Windows).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No more clobbered fresh state.</strong> Syncing from the
          keychain used to overwrite newer in-memory tokens with a stale
          keychain blob. Now it only adopts keychain state when it's actually
          newer, and auto-detects when Claude Code's own <code>/login</code>
          switched you into a different captured account.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ ADDED ============ -->
  <section class="wn-section section-soft">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <h2 class="h-section fade-up">Added</h2>
      <ul class="wn-list fade-up">
        <li><strong>Linux and Windows, for real.</strong> Native tray icon, OS-native credential storage (Secret Service / Credential Manager), and autostart on both — the same menu and auto-swap you get on macOS.</li>
        <li><strong>Codex switching.</strong> Swap between OpenAI Codex accounts the same way, on all three OSes. <code>~/.codex/auth.json</code> is rewritten atomically under usagio's control.</li>
        <li><strong>Menu redesign.</strong> A flatter main list (provider, email, session %, weekly %), cleaner account submenus, and a proper Settings ▸ tree for notifications, auto-swap threshold, and backups.</li>
        <li><strong>macOS <code>.app</code> bundle.</strong> Login Items in System Settings now shows the usagio icon instead of a generic exec glyph.</li>
        <li><strong>Adaptive poll cadence.</strong> Polling tightens as an account approaches its auto-swap trigger threshold, so a fast climb toward the wall gets caught sooner.</li>
        <li><strong>Backups ▸ Save… / Restore…</strong> via native OS file dialogs, with automatic pre-restore snapshots.</li>
        <li><strong>Settings ▸ Notifications ▸.</strong> Per-trigger toggles for threshold, reset-back, and weekly-pace alerts.</li>
        <li><strong>Full CI matrix.</strong> Every push is built, linted, and tested on macOS, Linux, and Windows, including live tray, credential-store, and autostart round-trips.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ REMOVED ============ -->
  <section class="wn-section">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <h2 class="h-section fade-up">Removed</h2>
      <ul class="wn-list fade-up">
        <li><strong>The "Launch at login" menu checkbox.</strong> It re-prompted for macOS Automation permission on every <code>brew upgrade</code>. Autostart is CLI-only now: <code>usagio install</code> / <code>usagio uninstall</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>~1,400 lines of over-engineered token-sync machinery.</strong> Collapsed to one refresher, one keychain reader, one mirror-back method — the design now has a single owner for each piece of state.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ MIGRATION ============ -->
  <section class="wn-section section-soft">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <h2 class="h-section fade-up">Upgrading</h2>
      <p class="lede fade-up" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Nothing to reconfigure. State and keychain items carry over unchanged;
        first launch silently mirrors the active account's token back to the
        keychain to close any pre-existing drift.
      </p>
      <ul class="wn-list fade-up">
        <li><strong>macOS:</strong> <code>brew upgrade</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Linux:</strong> <code>brew upgrade</code> via linuxbrew, or download the new tarball from the releases page.</li>
        <li><strong>Windows:</strong> download the new zip from the releases page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="wn-foot fade-up">
        <a href={changelog} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Full CHANGELOG on GitHub →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .wn-hero {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem) 0 clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(70% 60% at 50% 0%, rgba(91,43,234,0.06), transparent 65%),
      var(--bg);
    border-bottom: var(--hairline);
  }
  .wn-hero code,
  .wn-list code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--accent-tint);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .wn-section { padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem) 0; }
  .wn-section .h-section { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .wn-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .wn-list li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .wn-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.55em;
    width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .wn-list li strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 650; }
  .wn-foot { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .wn-foot a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .wn-foot a:hover { color: var(--accent-hover); }
</style>
